  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1 & =0 \\\\ -\\sqrt[9]{9-12x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{9-12x} & =-1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[9]{9-12x})^{9} & =(-1)^{9} \\\\ 9-12x & =-1 \\\\ -12x & =-10 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{5}{6}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
